    {
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "channel": "stable",
      "date": "2026-09-29",
      "status": "available",
      "source": {
        "repository": "https://github.com/DreamWeave-MP/dream_path",
        "tag": "1.0.0",
        "revision": "b3d33ea9cfa8c9a214296b6645e091a16b242c21"
      },
      "notes": {
        "summary": "First stable release: the Luau API is an l3i extension providing @dream/path, normalization is faster, and the Rust and Luau APIs are under semver.",
        "migration": "Compose `dream_path::lua::PathExtension` into the host's `RuntimePlan`. A host that still wants the\n`dreamPath` global adds `RuntimePolicy::compat_global(\"@dream/path\", \"dreamPath\")`. The functions\nand their results are unchanged.\n",
        "changed": [
          "An already-normalized path is copied as one block, and the rest folded without branches: a normalized 56-byte key costs 36 ns instead of 91 ns.",
          "A Luau call reads its path as a borrowed view and normalizes into a per-thread buffer, allocating nothing after warm-up; calls take about half as long as with `mlua`.",
          "The definitions check and the strict-script test build behind the `luau-analysis` feature (`cargo test --features luau-analysis`); `cargo test --features lua` does not build Luau's analysis frontend.",
          "l3i 1.0.0 comes from crates.io."
        ],
        "breaking": [
          "The `lua` feature binds the crate as an l3i extension, `lua::PathExtension`, providing the module `@dream/path`. `create_module`, `register_module`, `register_module_as` and the `standalone-lua` feature are gone with `mlua`.",
          "Building with the `lua` feature needs l3i's toolchain: clang, lld and cross-language thin LTO.",
          "Rust 1.92."
        ]
      },
